---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Image from "astro/components/Image.astro";

import aboutImage from "../assets/about.jpg";
import logoImage from "../assets/logo.png";
---

<Layout title="About" img={aboutImage} alt="SBSB performing on stage">
  <div class="flex flex-col items-center justify-start">
    <h1 class="text-5xl">About</h1>
    <Image src={logoImage} alt="SBSB logo" />
  </div>
  <div class="mt-10 flex flex-col items-center justify-start gap-5">
    <div
      class="flex flex-col gap-5 rounded-2xl bg-[#00000055] p-5 text-lg backdrop-blur-lg"
    >
      <p class="max-w-3xl">
        Something Borrowed Something Blue is Duke University&apos;s co-ed
        Christian a cappella group, consisting of students who love God and love
        to sing. Originally founded in 1969 as a Christian folk band, SBSB
        became an a cappella group in 1993 and adopted a new wedding-themed name
        in 1998 to remind us that we, as the church, are the beloved bride of
        Christ (Revelation 21). We exist primarily to glorify God and choose to
        perform a wide variety of songs to communicate the love of Christ. Our
        repertoire reflects aspects of God's character and includes music that
        has meaningfully influenced our members' lives. Singing, however, is
        just one part of being a member of SBSB — from vivacious game nights to
        our annual Spring Break community service trip, SBSB blends fun,
        service, and music, allowing us to grow as followers of Christ and as a
        family of friends.
      </p>
      <p class="max-w-3xl">
        SBSB is proud to be comprised of students of all different backgrounds
        and identities. We are dedicated to loving one another as members of one
        body in Christ following 1 John 4:7-21. Thus, SBSB adheres to Duke's
        policy of non-discrimination and harassment: any discrimination and/or
        harassment based on race, color, national origin, sex (including
        pregnancy), gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual
        orientation, religion, genetic information, age, disability, or veteran
        status is prohibited.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
